remise 7).\n2. **Implications of Roughness**: Rough things are green or red (Premise 10).  \n   - Fiona cannot be red (Premise 6), so she must be **green**.\n3. **Green Coloring**: Green things are not blue (Premise 8).  \n   - Therefore, **Fiona is not blue**.\n\n**Contradiction Check**: Assuming Fiona were blue would lead to inconsistencies:\n- If Fiona were blue (Premise 11), she\u2019d be **kind**, but Premise 14 states rough, red things are kind.  \n   - Fiona is green (not red), so being rough and green contradicts being kind if she were blue.  \n\nThus, Fiona\u2019s color is **green**, not blue. The statement \"Fiona is blue\" is **false**.\n\n**Answer**: \\boxed{B}",
